{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:97e20a9f6957ebfb","name":"Hooligan","source":{"id":"source:reference-97e20a9f6957ebfb","title":"Hooligan","revision":19683,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:24:53Z","sha256":"b08321661437e0b465deee06d301d9a2192941e931224ec4fda563b3598873a7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19683","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Hooligan&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-97e20a9f6957ebfb","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["These four youths are huddled around a small table, each one nursing a tall blue cup filled with some type of alcoholic drink. Their clothes are rumpled, and they appear to be scruffy. They talk a little too loudly, trying to look tough."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["These four Hooligans are typical Mos Eisley street trash. They have come to the Woodoo Dunes for a few cheap drinks and maybe a little bit of action. They are all coming down from a ryll high, and none of them is in the mood for idle chatter. If they see an opportunity to score free spice, they side with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cel N'ero"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cel_N%27ero","referenceId":"reference:d8c7e2597c283e1d"},", who is a known dealer, regardless of how much the odds are stacked against them.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Hooligans shoot at random targets. They do not coordinate their attacks, and they are not concerned with collateral damage they might cause. If more than half their number are killed or incapacitated, the survivors attempt to flee, shooting as they go.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Hooligan Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2b